Purpose
This file is the bridge between `ocaml-agent-graph` and an external BulkheadLM server.

Linear intent
1. Define small local records for token usage and completion output so the rest of the framework gets a simple normalized shape.
2. Define the client state around one resolved authorization header, discovered route metadata, and either an external HTTP transport or a test-only embedded store.
3. Resolve the authorization header either from an inline token or from an environment variable.
4. Create a client by contacting the external BulkheadLM server, reading `/v1/models`, and indexing the available routes.
5. Expose `of_store` so tests can still inject a mocked BulkheadLM runtime without hitting the network.
6. Extract the useful text from the normalized BulkheadLM chat response choices.
7. Build a chat request from the agent profile and prompt messages.
8. Send normal runtime requests to the external BulkheadLM `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint, while keeping the embedded dispatch path only for isolated tests.
9. Convert BulkheadLM HTTP or runtime errors into plain error strings and successful responses into the local normalized completion shape.
